{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>לבד [alone].</b> Joined to a feminine form, yet it is masculine. The sense: that Elohim made man to be upright, walking in the way, but they sought out crooked paths. And this matter is also connected to the verse above: one woman is enough for a man."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:28:16.273382275Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}